# Scorched Hemp -- decarboxylated hemp, cooked past the point of use.
#
# The MATRIX is item/decarboxylated_hemp.png extracted verbatim; only the PALETTE is ours. Same
# heap, same five tones in the same luminance order, pushed from olive to a charred brown. That is
# the whole visual idea: it is the same material, only worse, and a player who has seen the oven's
# output should read this as "that, burnt" before reading the name.
#
# The green goes entirely. Heat breaks chlorophyll down to brown pheophytin, which is the real
# reason this item cannot be washed -- there is no green left in it for water to take out.
# Each tone sits a little darker than the one it replaces, so the two items stay apart at 1:1 in a
# hotbar and not only at zoom.
#
# PLACEHOLDER: derived art, not drawn. Redraw or retone freely.

@palette scorched
. = none
1 = 120D09
2 = 2A1D14
3 = 44301F
4 = 614329
5 = 855E38

@texture item/scorched_hemp 16x16 palette=scorched type=item
